# tools/s/sundial.rish — accrete shim → tools/gen/season/sundial.rish (Generator Season s4)
# NAME NOTE (`20260821.175633`). This meter is named **Plumb** -- a plumb line tells you whether a
# thing is true, which is what this reads of a recursion prompt. It wore the word `sundial` until
# the vocabulary pruning found two live meters under one name, told apart only by a capital
# letter: the health face `sundial/sundial.rye` keeps **Sundial**, and this one became Plumb.
# The FILE keeps its elder name because seven living files call it by that path, and a promise
# kept is worth more than a tidy filename -- the same reason tools/rye/session_logs_archive.rye kept
# its name when its destination molted.
if length args == 0 then let r = run ["rishi/bin/rishi" "run" "tools/gen/season/sundial.rish"]
if length args != 0 then let r = run ["rishi/bin/rishi" "run" "tools/gen/season/sundial.rish" args[0]]
if r.out != "" then say r.out
exit r.code
